+//! Pleiades: at least one object imaged by Pleiades 1A on 23 March 2014 came from 9M-MRO.
+//!
+//! **Source.** Geoscience Australia examined four Pleiades 1A scenes taken at about 04:00 UTC on
+//! 23 March 2014 near 35°S 91°E (Minchin et al. 2017, GA Record 2017/13). It rated 12 of 70 objects
+//! "probably man-made" but could not say whether they are aircraft debris. Griffin & Oke (2017, CSIRO
+//! EP174155) postulated that some are, and asked where the aircraft entered the water. This module
+//! asks the same question as an explicit conditional alternative, never as the base estimate.
+//!
+//! **Data.** `objects.csv` transcribes GA Tables 1-4. PHR_2 object 12 is printed with latitude and
+//! longitude swapped and is corrected. The 12 rating-5 objects lie at four places: PHR4N (objects
+//! 2-6), PHR4S (18, 19, 26, 27), PHR3 (7, 10) and PHR1 (1). Objects in a cluster are within 6 km of
+//! each other, far below the transport error, so each cluster is one observation at its centroid.
+//! [`SCENES`] are the footprints, read from GA Fig. 2 after georeferencing it with the 70 object
+//! markers (median residual 0.3 km). The figure is plate carrée with equal degrees per pixel. The
+//! four boxes are about 17 x 25 km each, total A = 1,773 km²; GA's text says "approximately 25 km x
+//! 20 km".
+//!
+//! **Likelihood.** For an impact at s, an ocean model and a windage factor, a floating item's
+//! position at 04:00 UTC on 23 March is x(s) + e:
+//! - x(s) is the deterministic surface-drift endpoint from the drift maps built offline by
+//!   crates/ocean (current + windage x ERA5 10 m wind, no explicit Stokes; RK2 on WGS-84, 1 h
+//!   step), interpolated bilinearly in s. A 0.0125° map covers 42-32°S 82-96°E, which holds 99.3%
+//!   of the base 00:19 posterior. It blends over 0.25° into a 0.05° map covering 50-15°S 70-115°E.
+//!   Against direct integration, bilinear interpolation is off by p95 <= 1.2 km at 0.0125° (GLORYS12;
+//!   BRAN2016 0.6, OSCAR 0.2) and 14-19 km at 0.05°. A few sources per thousand sit on eddy
+//!   separatrices, where the deterministic endpoint is ill-conditioned; the kernel covers that. In a
+//!   stand-in on the base 00:19 posterior, using the 0.05° maps alone changed Z_H by at most 0.2%
+//!   and left the latitude summaries unchanged, so the coarse fallback outside the box is adequate.
+//!   Both maps are built at crates/ocean revision 2724f57, after an ERA5 wind-extraction fix;
+//! - e is the 15-day transport error, an isotropic bivariate Student-t (or Gaussian) with density
+//!   p(e).
+//!
+//! If not-H, the cluster positions are uniform over the footprint (density 1/A). If H, exactly one
+//! cluster c is MRO debris (single association), with equal weights w_c, and the rest are background:
+//!
+//!   Λ_H(s) = p(y | s, H) / p(y | not-H) = Σ_c w_c · A · p(y_c − x(s)).
+//!
+//! The module returns ln Λ_H for H and 0 for not-H. Both are ratios against the same background, so
+//! the composer can mix them. The likelihood is analytic and seed-free, with no floor. An impact
+//! outside the drift map, or one whose drift left the ocean domain, is NaN (not computed).
+//!
+//! **What π means.** Suppose MRO left K detectable floating debris groups, each drifting
+//! independently with density p, each seen with probability η when inside a scene, and background
+//! objects form a Poisson process of intensity n/A over the scenes. In the sparse limit the Poisson
+//! likelihood ratio is then 1 + Kη · Λ_H(s). The composer's mixture (1 − π) + π · Λ_H(s) is the same
+//! up to a constant, with prior odds π / (1 − π) = Kη: the expected number of MRO objects big enough
+//! to be rated 5 that would be seen if the whole debris field were imaged. It is not the everyday
+//! "chance that an imaged object is MRO". That is roughly Kη · P_F, and P_F, the chance that one
+//! item lands inside the 1,773 km² footprint, is at most A / (2π · scale²) ≈ 5.4% at the
+//! calibrated error (OSCAR's 72 km scale). The Poisson term for MRO debris that should have been
+//! seen but wasn't, −Kη · P_F(s), is dropped: it is at most 0.054 Kη in ln Λ, negligible for
+//! Kη ≲ 5.
+//!
+//! **How weak a 15-day back-track is.** Against drifters, GLORYS12 and BRAN2016 currents alone
+//! predict 15-day displacement barely better than assuming no motion (skill 0.10 and 0.08 for
+//! drogued drifters; OSCAR's 30 m mean reaches 0.44). With 1.2% ERA5 windage, undrogued drifters
+//! reach skill 0.49-0.60, with Student-t errors of scale 72-94 km (RMS 118-133 km per
+//! component). So even if H holds, the images locate the impact only to within a few hundred
+//! kilometres. The deterministic endpoint map also carries eddy-scale structure the
+//! model cannot forecast, and those details differ between ocean models. That is why the ocean
+//! model is an alternative weighed by evidence, not a fixed choice.
+//!
+//! **Transport error (15 days).** The kernel comes from the crates/ocean GDP replay (Ocean drift
+//! thread, revision 2724f57, report/drift_replay.py): 2014 drifters in 25-45°S 60-115°E, 15-day
+//! segments starting every 3 days, with the drift map's integrator and fields.
+//! - Primary, per ocean model: undrogued drifters with current + 1.2% ERA5 wind (n = 1,207),
+//!   Student-t ν / scale / skill: GLORYS12 2.73 / 77.3 km / 0.56, OSCAR 2.62 / 72.3 km / 0.60,
+//!   BRAN2016 3.68 / 94.1 km / 0.49. It measures the transport error for an object whose leeway
+//!   is modelled correctly, so every windage class uses it. At 3%, the ERA5 wind error (about
+//!   1.5 m/s) would add roughly 30 km in quadrature over 15 days, which is small beside 72-94 km.
+//! - The mismatched configurations are wider. Current-only drogued is 98 / 68 / 101 km: a 15 m
+//!   drogue against the top model level. 3% windage on undrogued drifters is 117 / 87 / 117 km:
+//!   drifters are not 3% objects.
+//! - Conservative sensitivity: a pooled current-only GLORYS12 fit (drogued + undrogued, from an
+//!   independent exploratory calibration that matched the replay's current-only rows),
+//!   Student-t ν 3.75, 107 km, or a Gaussian σ 146 km.
+//! - The drifters feel the same unresolved dispersion as debris, so no random walk is added.
+//! - The Pleiades horizon is 15.14 days; the calibration uses 15.0 days, a difference under 1% in
+//!   scale.
+//!
+//! **Departures from Griffin & Oke (2017).** They ranked four candidate strips qualitatively, using
+//! BRAN2015/2016, a 5 NM/day random walk (25 km per component at 15 days) and windage 0, 1.2% and 3%.
+//! They kept only findings both models supported, and did not normalise against a background. This
+//! module departs as follows:
+//! - the likelihood ratio is explicit, with the footprint background;
+//! - the error is drifter-calibrated, about 3x wider than their random walk;
+//! - ocean model and windage are alternatives weighed by evidence, not discarded when models disagree.
+//!
+//! Their 1.2% windage is treated as the Stokes proxy they describe, so no WAVERYS Stokes is added.
+//!
+//! **Release time.** The drift maps release at 00:40 UTC on 8 March. An impact at another time
+//! would release its debris earlier or later, which moves the endpoint by at most |u| · Δt. The
+//! fastest object speed over the map grid on 8 March 00:00-01:00 is 1.35 m/s (GLORYS12, 3%
+//! windage; drift-map manifests). |d ln p / dr| peaks at (ν + 2) / (2 √ν · scale), at most 0.020
+//! per km (OSCAR). So ln Λ_H changes by at most 0.0016 per minute of offset: under 0.05 for the
+//! 00:20-01:10 impacts of the end-of-flight endings, and under 0.15 at the ±90 min limit.
+//! Typical speeds (0.3-0.6 m/s) give a third of that. Impacts further from 00:40, or without a
+//! time, are not computed.
+//!
+//! **Sensitivities** (run.toml parameters):
+//! - `association = { kind = "at-least-one", rho }`: each cluster is independently MRO with
+//!   probability ρ, conditioned on at least one:
+//!   Λ = [Π_c((1 − ρ) + ρ · A · p_c) − (1 − ρ)^n] / [1 − (1 − ρ)^n].
+//!   It tends to the single form as ρ → 0 and to the product Π_c A · p_c at ρ = 1. The MRO clusters
+//!   are drawn independently, with no shared model error.
+//! - `min_rating = 4`: the 39 objects rated 4 or 5, grouped by scene (adds PHR_2).
+//! - `kernel`: the pooled current-only Student-t (ν 3.75, 107 km) or a Gaussian (σ 146 km).
+
+use hypothesis::{Alternatives, Hypothesis, ImpactView};
+use serde::Deserialize;
+use std::collections::BTreeMap;
+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
+
+/// GA Tables 1-4 (70 objects), with PHR_2 object 12 corrected.
+const OBJECTS: &str = include_str!("objects.csv");
+
+/// Scene footprints [south, north, west, east] in degrees, from GA Fig. 2 (see the module comment).
+pub const SCENES: [(&str, [f64; 4]); 4] = [
+    ("PHR_1", [-35.402, -35.155, 90.388, 90.581]),
+    ("PHR_2", [-35.387, -35.158, 91.233, 91.425]),
+    ("PHR_3", [-34.640, -34.416, 90.396, 90.578]),
+    ("PHR_4", [-34.636, -34.411, 91.233, 91.422]),
+];
+
+/// Drift-map release and endpoint times. The endpoint is GA/CSIRO's "~4Z".
+const RELEASE_UTC: &str = "2014-03-08T00:40:00Z";
+const END_UTC: &str = "2014-03-23T04:00:00Z";
+/// The release time as Unix seconds, and how far from it an impact may be before the map no
+/// longer applies (see "Release time" above).
+const RELEASE_UNIX_S: f64 = 1_394_239_200.0;
+const RELEASE_WINDOW_S: f64 = 5_400.0;
+
+/// Axis label for the composer's prior sweep of H (see "What π means").
+const SWEEP_LABEL: &str = "expected detectable rating-5-sized MRO objects K·η (prior odds of H)";
+
+/// IUGG mean Earth radius. Haversine distances agree with the WGS-84 geodesic to <0.01% here.
+const EARTH_RADIUS_KM: f64 = 6_371.008_8;
+
+#[derive(Deserialize)]
+#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]
+struct Params {
+    /// Drift-map directories: one list per ocean model, finest map first, each relative to the
+    /// working directory (`make` runs from the repository root).
+    drift_maps: Vec<Vec<PathBuf>>,
+    /// 15-day transport error for each ocean model, keyed by the model name in its manifest.
+    kernel: BTreeMap<String, Kernel>,
+    #[serde(default = "default_min_rating")]
+    min_rating: u8,
+    #[serde(default)]
+    association: Association,
+}
+
+fn default_min_rating() -> u8 {
+    5
+}
+
+/// Isotropic bivariate transport-error density, as a function of distance r (km).
+#[derive(Deserialize, Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq)]
+#[serde(tag = "form", rename_all = "kebab-case", deny_unknown_fields)]
+pub enum Kernel {
+    StudentT { nu: f64, scale_km: f64 },
+    Gaussian { sigma_km: f64 },
+}
+
+impl Kernel {
+    /// ln p(e) per km² at |e| = r km, normalised over the plane.
+    pub fn ln_density(self, r_km: f64) -> f64 {
+        match self {
+            Kernel::StudentT { nu, scale_km: s } => {
+                -(2.0 * std::f64::consts::PI * s * s).ln() - 0.5 * (nu + 2.0) * (r_km * r_km / (nu * s * s)).ln_1p()
+            }
+            Kernel::Gaussian { sigma_km: s } => -(2.0 * std::f64::consts::PI * s * s).ln() - 0.5 * r_km * r_km / (s * s),
+        }
+    }
+
+    fn validate(self) -> Result<Self, String> {
+        let ok = match self {
+            Kernel::StudentT { nu, scale_km } => nu > 0.0 && scale_km > 0.0,
+            Kernel::Gaussian { sigma_km } => sigma_km > 0.0,
+        };
+        if ok { Ok(self) } else { Err(format!("pleiades: invalid kernel {self:?}")) }
+    }
+}
+
+/// How the clusters relate to H (see the module comment).
+#[derive(Deserialize, Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq)]
+#[serde(tag = "kind", rename_all = "kebab-case", deny_unknown_fields)]
+pub enum Association {
+    #[default]
+    Single,
+    AtLeastOne { rho: f64 },
+}
+
+/// One observation: the centroid of a group of imaged objects.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]
+pub struct Cluster {
+    pub id: String,
+    pub latitude_deg: f64,
+    pub longitude_deg: f64,
+    pub objects: usize,
+}
+
+/// One row of `objects.csv`.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]
+pub struct Object {
+    pub scene: String,
+    pub number: u32,
+    pub latitude_deg: f64,
+    pub longitude_deg: f64,
+    pub rating: u8,
+    pub cluster: String,
+}
+
+pub fn objects() -> Vec<Object> {
+    OBJECTS
+        .lines()
+        .filter(|l| !l.starts_with('#'))
+        .skip(1)
+        .map(|l| {
+            let f: Vec<&str> = l.split(',').collect();
+            Object {
+                scene: f[0].to_string(),
+                number: f[1].parse().unwrap(),
+                latitude_deg: f[2].parse().unwrap(),
+                longitude_deg: f[3].parse().unwrap(),
+                rating: f[6].parse().unwrap(),
+                cluster: f[7].to_string(),
+            }
+        })
+        .collect()
+}
+
+/// Rating 5: the four named clusters. Rating >= 4: one cluster per scene.
+pub fn clusters(min_rating: u8) -> Result<Vec<Cluster>, String> {
+    let key = |o: &Object| match min_rating {
+        5 => o.cluster.clone(),
+        _ => o.scene.replace('_', ""),
+    };
+    if !(min_rating == 4 || min_rating == 5) {
+        return Err(format!("pleiades: min_rating must be 4 or 5, not {min_rating}"));
+    }
+    let mut groups: BTreeMap<String, Vec<Object>> = BTreeMap::new();
+    for o in objects().into_iter().filter(|o| o.rating >= min_rating) {
+        groups.entry(key(&o)).or_default().push(o);
+    }
+    Ok(groups
+        .into_iter()
+        .map(|(id, members)| {
+            let n = members.len() as f64;
+            Cluster {
+                id,
+                latitude_deg: members.iter().map(|o| o.latitude_deg).sum::<f64>() / n,
+                longitude_deg: members.iter().map(|o| o.longitude_deg).sum::<f64>() / n,
+                objects: members.len(),
+            }
+        })
+        .collect())
+}
+
+/// Total footprint area (km²) on the sphere: R² (sin φn − sin φs) Δλ per box.
+pub fn footprint_area_km2() -> f64 {
+    SCENES
+        .iter()
+        .map(|(_, [s, n, w, e])| {
+            EARTH_RADIUS_KM.powi(2) * (n.to_radians().sin() - s.to_radians().sin()) * (e - w).to_radians()
+        })
+        .sum()
+}
+
+pub fn distance_km(lat1: f64, lon1: f64, lat2: f64, lon2: f64) -> f64 {
+    let (p1, p2) = (lat1.to_radians(), lat2.to_radians());
+    let h = ((p2 - p1) / 2.0).sin().powi(2) + p1.cos() * p2.cos() * ((lon2 - lon1).to_radians() / 2.0).sin().powi(2);
+    2.0 * EARTH_RADIUS_KM * h.sqrt().min(1.0).asin()
+}
+
+/// Deterministic drift endpoints on a regular source grid, for one ocean model and several windage
+/// factors (built offline by crates/ocean; `manifest.toml` + little-endian f32 arrays).
+pub struct DriftMap {
+    pub model: String,
+    lat0: f64,
+    lon0: f64,
+    step: f64,
+    nlat: usize,
+    nlon: usize,
+    pub windage: Vec<f64>,
+    /// Per windage: end latitude and end longitude, row-major, latitude ascending; NaN = not computed.
+    end: Vec<(Vec<f32>, Vec<f32>)>,
+}
+
+#[derive(Deserialize)]
+struct Manifest {
+    model: String,
+    release_utc: String,
+    end_utc: String,
+    lat0_deg: f64,
+    lon0_deg: f64,
+    step_deg: f64,
+    nlat: usize,
+    nlon: usize,
+    windage: Vec<f64>,
+    latitude_files: Vec<String>,
+    longitude_files: Vec<String>,
+}
+
+impl DriftMap {
+    pub fn load(dir: &Path) -> Result<Self, String> {
+        let path = dir.join("manifest.toml");
+        let text = std::fs::read_to_string(&path).map_err(|e| format!("pleiades: {}: {e}", path.display()))?;
+        let m: Manifest = toml::from_str(&text).map_err(|e| format!("pleiades: {}: {e}", path.display()))?;
+        if m.release_utc != RELEASE_UTC || m.end_utc != END_UTC {
+            return Err(format!("pleiades: {} runs {} -> {}, expected {RELEASE_UTC} -> {END_UTC}", path.display(), m.release_utc, m.end_utc));
+        }
+        if m.latitude_files.len() != m.windage.len() || m.longitude_files.len() != m.windage.len() {
+            return Err(format!("pleiades: {}: one latitude and one longitude file per windage", path.display()));
+        }
+        let read = |name: &str| -> Result<Vec<f32>, String> {
+            let p = dir.join(name);
+            let bytes = std::fs::read(&p).map_err(|e| format!("pleiades: {}: {e}", p.display()))?;
+            if bytes.len() != 4 * m.nlat * m.nlon {
+                return Err(format!("pleiades: {} has {} bytes, expected {}", p.display(), bytes.len(), 4 * m.nlat * m.nlon));
+            }
+            Ok(bytes.as_chunks::<4>().0.iter().map(|b| f32::from_le_bytes(*b)).collect())
+        };
+        let end = m
+            .latitude_files
+            .iter()
+            .zip(&m.longitude_files)
+            .map(|(la, lo)| Ok((read(la)?, read(lo)?)))
+            .collect::<Result<_, String>>()?;
+        Self::new(m.model, [m.lat0_deg, m.lon0_deg, m.step_deg], [m.nlat, m.nlon], m.windage, end)
+    }
+
+    pub fn new(model: String, origin_step: [f64; 3], shape: [usize; 2], windage: Vec<f64>, end: Vec<(Vec<f32>, Vec<f32>)>) -> Result<Self, String> {
+        let [lat0, lon0, step] = origin_step;
+        let [nlat, nlon] = shape;
+        if !(step > 0.0 && nlat >= 2 && nlon >= 2) || end.len() != windage.len() || end.iter().any(|(a, b)| a.len() != nlat * nlon || b.len() != nlat * nlon) {
+            return Err(format!("pleiades: drift map {model}: inconsistent grid"));
+        }
+        Ok(Self { model, lat0, lon0, step, nlat, nlon, windage, end })
+    }
+
+    /// 1 at least `margin` degrees inside the grid's box, falling linearly to 0 at its edge.
+    fn inside_weight(&self, lat: f64, lon: f64, margin: f64) -> f64 {
+        let (lat1, lon1) = (self.lat0 + self.step * (self.nlat - 1) as f64, self.lon0 + self.step * (self.nlon - 1) as f64);
+        let d = (lat - self.lat0).min(lat1 - lat).min(lon - self.lon0).min(lon1 - lon);
+        (d / margin).clamp(0.0, 1.0)
+    }
+
+    /// Bilinearly interpolated endpoint (lat, lon) for a source at (lat, lon); None if the source is
+    /// outside the grid or any surrounding node was not computed.
+    pub fn endpoint(&self, w: usize, lat: f64, lon: f64) -> Option<(f64, f64)> {
+        let fi = (lat - self.lat0) / self.step;
+        let fj = (lon - self.lon0) / self.step;
+        if !(fi >= 0.0 && fj >= 0.0 && fi <= (self.nlat - 1) as f64 && fj <= (self.nlon - 1) as f64) {
+            return None;
+        }
+        let (i, j) = ((fi as usize).min(self.nlat - 2), (fj as usize).min(self.nlon - 2));
+        let (a, b) = (fi - i as f64, fj - j as f64);
+        let (ends_lat, ends_lon) = &self.end[w];
+        let interp = |v: &[f32]| {
+            let at = |ii: usize, jj: usize| f64::from(v[ii * self.nlon + jj]);
+            (1.0 - a) * ((1.0 - b) * at(i, j) + b * at(i, j + 1)) + a * ((1.0 - b) * at(i + 1, j) + b * at(i + 1, j + 1))
+        };
+        let (la, lo) = (interp(ends_lat), interp(ends_lon));
+        (la.is_finite() && lo.is_finite()).then_some((la, lo))
+    }
+}
+
+/// One ocean model's drift maps, finest first. A finer map is used where it applies; over the
+/// last [`BLEND_MARGIN_DEG`] inside its edge it blends linearly into the next coarser map, so the
+/// endpoint, and the likelihood, stay continuous across the boundary.
+pub struct DriftModel {
+    pub levels: Vec<DriftMap>,
+}
+
+/// Width of the fine-to-coarse blend inside a finer map's edge.
+pub const BLEND_MARGIN_DEG: f64 = 0.25;
+
+impl DriftModel {
+    pub fn new(levels: Vec<DriftMap>) -> Result<Self, String> {
+        let first = levels.first().ok_or("pleiades: an ocean model needs at least one drift map")?;
+        if levels.iter().any(|m| m.model != first.model || m.windage != first.windage) {
+            return Err(format!("pleiades: drift maps for {} disagree on model or windage", first.model));
+        }
+        Ok(Self { levels })
+    }
+
+    pub fn name(&self) -> &str {
+        &self.levels[0].model
+    }
+
+    pub fn endpoint(&self, w: usize, lat: f64, lon: f64) -> Option<(f64, f64)> {
+        Self::blended(&self.levels, w, lat, lon)
+    }
+
+    fn blended(levels: &[DriftMap], w: usize, lat: f64, lon: f64) -> Option<(f64, f64)> {
+        let (fine, coarser) = levels.split_first()?;
+        if coarser.is_empty() {
+            return fine.endpoint(w, lat, lon);
+        }
+        let f = fine.inside_weight(lat, lon, BLEND_MARGIN_DEG);
+        if f >= 1.0 {
+            return fine.endpoint(w, lat, lon);
+        }
+        let coarse = Self::blended(coarser, w, lat, lon);
+        if f <= 0.0 {
+            return coarse;
+        }
+        let ((a, b), (c, d)) = (fine.endpoint(w, lat, lon)?, coarse?);
+        Some((f * a + (1.0 - f) * c, f * b + (1.0 - f) * d))
+    }
+}
+
+pub struct Pleiades {
+    pub clusters: Vec<Cluster>,
+    pub area_km2: f64,
+    pub models: Vec<DriftModel>,
+    kernels: Vec<Kernel>,
+    association: Association,
+}
+
+pub fn new(params: &toml::Value) -> Result<Box<dyn Hypothesis>, String> {
+    let params: Params = params.clone().try_into().map_err(|e| format!("pleiades: {e}"))?;
+    let models = params
+        .drift_maps
+        .iter()
+        .map(|dirs| DriftModel::new(dirs.iter().map(|d| DriftMap::load(d)).collect::<Result<_, _>>()?))
+        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?;
+    Ok(Box::new(Pleiades::new(models, &params.kernel, params.min_rating, params.association)?))
+}
+
+impl Pleiades {
+    pub fn new(models: Vec<DriftModel>, kernels: &BTreeMap<String, Kernel>, min_rating: u8, association: Association) -> Result<Self, String> {
+        if models.is_empty() {
+            return Err("pleiades: no drift maps".into());
+        }
+        if let Association::AtLeastOne { rho } = association {
+            if !(rho > 0.0 && rho <= 1.0) {
+                return Err(format!("pleiades: rho must be in (0, 1], not {rho}"));
+            }
+        }
+        let kernels = models
+            .iter()
+            .map(|m| kernels.get(m.name()).copied().ok_or(format!("pleiades: no kernel for ocean model {}", m.name()))?.validate())
+            .collect::<Result<_, _>>()?;
+        if models.iter().any(|m| m.levels[0].windage != models[0].levels[0].windage) {
+            return Err("pleiades: every drift map must carry the same windage factors".into());
+        }
+        Ok(Self { clusters: clusters(min_rating)?, area_km2: footprint_area_km2(), models, kernels, association })
+    }
+
+    /// Observations consumed, once per run.
+    pub fn observation_ids(&self) -> Vec<String> {
+        self.clusters.iter().map(|c| format!("pleiades:{}", c.id)).collect()
+    }
+
+    /// The alternatives `impact_log_likelihood` distinguishes, in `choice` order: origin
+    /// {not-H, H} (prior odds 1, i.e. Kη = 1; the composer sweeps it), the shared ocean model,
+    /// and this module's windage. Priors are equal within each set.
+    pub fn alternative_sets(&self) -> Vec<Alternatives> {
+        let equal = |name: &str, labels: Vec<String>| {
+            let p = 1.0 / labels.len() as f64;
+            Alternatives { name: name.into(), options: labels.into_iter().map(|l| (l, p)).collect(), sweep_label: None }
+        };
+        let mut origin = equal("pleiades-origin", vec!["not-H".into(), "H".into()]);
+        origin.sweep_label = Some(SWEEP_LABEL.into());
+        vec![
+            origin,
+            equal("ocean-model", self.models.iter().map(|m| m.name().to_string()).collect()),
+            equal("pleiades-windage", self.models[0].levels[0].windage.iter().map(|w| format!("{w}")).collect()),
+        ]
+    }
+
+    /// ln p(data | impact, choice) relative to the background: 0 for not-H, ln Λ_H for H.
+    pub fn log_likelihood(&self, choice: &[usize], latitude_deg: f64, longitude_deg: f64) -> f64 {
+        let [origin, m, w] = choice else { panic!("pleiades: choice needs 3 indices, got {choice:?}") };
+        if *origin == 0 { 0.0 } else { self.log_lambda_h(*m, *w, latitude_deg, longitude_deg) }
+    }
+
+    /// ln Λ_H for an impact at (lat, lon) under ocean model `m` and windage `w`; ln Λ for not-H is 0.
+    /// NaN means not computed (outside the drift map, or the drift left the ocean domain).
+    pub fn log_lambda_h(&self, m: usize, w: usize, lat: f64, lon: f64) -> f64 {
+        let Some((end_lat, end_lon)) = self.models[m].endpoint(w, lat, lon) else {
+            return f64::NAN;
+        };
+        let ln_area = self.area_km2.ln();
+        // ln(A p_c) for each cluster.
+        let ln_a: Vec<f64> = self
+            .clusters
+            .iter()
+            .map(|c| ln_area + self.kernels[m].ln_density(distance_km(c.latitude_deg, c.longitude_deg, end_lat, end_lon)))
+            .collect();
+        combine(&ln_a, self.association)
+    }
+}
+
+/// ln Λ_H from ln(A p_c): the single-association mixture with equal weights, or the at-least-one
+/// form summed over non-empty subsets (no cancellation for small A p_c).
+pub fn combine(ln_a: &[f64], association: Association) -> f64 {
+    let n = ln_a.len();
+    match association {
+        Association::Single => log_sum_exp(ln_a.iter().copied()) - (n as f64).ln(),
+        Association::AtLeastOne { rho } => {
+            let (ln_rho, ln_not) = (rho.ln(), (1.0 - rho).ln());
+            let subsets = (1u32..1 << n).map(|mask| {
+                (0..n).map(|c| if mask & (1 << c) != 0 { ln_rho + ln_a[c] } else { ln_not }).sum::<f64>()
+            });
+            log_sum_exp(subsets) - (-(n as f64 * ln_not).exp()).ln_1p()
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+fn log_sum_exp(terms: impl Iterator<Item = f64> + Clone) -> f64 {
+    let max = terms.clone().fold(f64::NEG_INFINITY, f64::max);
+    if max == f64::NEG_INFINITY {
+        return max;
+    }
+    max + terms.map(|t| (t - max).exp()).sum::<f64>().ln()
+}
+
+/// An impact module: it acts only through the impact hooks, named in a `[[compose]]` set.
+impl Hypothesis for Pleiades {
+    fn observations(&self) -> Vec<String> {
+        self.observation_ids()
+    }
+
+    fn alternatives(&self) -> Vec<Alternatives> {
+        self.alternative_sets()
+    }
+
+    /// Both options are ratios against the same footprint background.
+    fn absolute_scale(&self) -> bool {
+        true
+    }
+
+    /// NaN (not computed) for an impact outside the drift maps, or more than
+    /// [`RELEASE_WINDOW_S`] from the maps' release time, or with no time.
+    fn impact_log_likelihood(&self, impact: &ImpactView, choice: &[usize]) -> f64 {
+        let offset = (impact.unix_s - RELEASE_UNIX_S).abs();
+        if offset.is_nan() || offset > RELEASE_WINDOW_S {
+            return f64::NAN;
+        }
+        self.log_likelihood(choice, impact.latitude_deg, impact.longitude_deg)
+    }
+}
